                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "61be7739-e997-31cf-8d55-838886116ace",
                        "entry_id": "1d0859d6-b874-339a-93d8-692a16450e8f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "helemaal niet mogelijk"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "691e7589-d64d-4d69-831c-62090f5a59c8",
                                "sense_id": "61be7739-e997-31cf-8d55-838886116ace",
                                "text": "In Making a Murderer 2 herhaalt Zellner keer op keer dat het godsonmogelijk is dat Avery en zijn neef Dassey verantwoordelijk zijn voor de brute moord op de fotografe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b56b90f3-fa69-43d6-bf10-c90f3cc1c6f6",
                                "sense_id": "61be7739-e997-31cf-8d55-838886116ace",
                                "text": "“Bestaat er iets dat nog stommer is dan sport?”, heeft Rudy Kousbroek zich wel eens afgevraagd. Kousbroeks eerste impuls was om te antwoorden: “Nee, dat kan niet, dat is godsonmogelijk.” Maar soms twijfelde hij en tenslotte kwam hij tot de conclusie dat “mode, tenminste in sommige aspecten, even erg is als voetbal”."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b949685-1a7d-479e-818d-e7dea8331fc3",
                        "source_entry_id": "1d0859d6-b874-339a-93d8-692a16450e8f",
                        "source_sense_id": "61be7739-e997-31cf-8d55-838886116ace",
                        "source_sense_description": "helemaal niet mogelijk",
                        "target_lang_word": "out of question",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "out of question",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48026979-b1a4-31e0-846b-1437af1daaa0",
                                        "entry_id": "7515fb4f-3bc2-3baa-b386-1454808e8fad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unquestionably, without question, certainly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2940f3a-6bcb-4d45-870a-61cef16890cc",
                                                "sense_id": "48026979-b1a4-31e0-846b-1437af1daaa0",
                                                "text": "Alas, Malvolio, this is not my writing,\nThough, I confess, much like the character\nBut out of question, ’tis Maria's hand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99b1b6e6-f9ff-4067-89d9-8ba2b1a15ba9",
                                                "sense_id": "48026979-b1a4-31e0-846b-1437af1daaa0",
                                                "text": "And out of question the cherfull help that may be in mariage toward sanctity of life, is the purest and so the noblest end of that contract […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0950324d-f506-4889-9b89-2c56be50e687",
                                                "sense_id": "48026979-b1a4-31e0-846b-1437af1daaa0",
                                                "text": "1772, Richard Hurd, letter addressed to Edward Gibbon dated 29 August, 1772, in Miscellaneous Works of Edward Gibbon, London: A. Strahan et al., p. 462,\n[…] the lustre of his hero’s fame, and the real power, which, out of question, he reserved to himself, would make us forget or overlook Cyaxares."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a2884e1-4ffb-3aef-8976-31b3aa1dae5d",
                                        "entry_id": "7515fb4f-3bc2-3baa-b386-1454808e8fad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unquestionable, beyond question, certain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f5c349e-67d2-454f-828a-6ea7cf92462d",
                                                "sense_id": "1a2884e1-4ffb-3aef-8976-31b3aa1dae5d",
                                                "text": "Of King Vaphres and Necho it is out of question, that neither of them was the great King Sesostris."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a194c69-0618-47fe-8907-1a20cc2ea2d4",
                                                "sense_id": "1a2884e1-4ffb-3aef-8976-31b3aa1dae5d",
                                                "text": "So when [Jesus] came walking upon the Sea to his Disciples, and they were so frighted that they cried out, believing that they had seen a Spirit; it must be out of Question that there were such things, and that they, the Disciples, had heard of them […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
